  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs8AAAABBPvD7A",
      "title": "ops: reject new Alt-DA chain configs",
      "author": "sbvegan",
      "number": 1318,
      "body": "Stops new Alt-DA registry intake while preserving exact metadata for the 12 deployed legacy chains. Rejects legacy op-deployer state before it can be silently rewritten.\n\nCompanion to ethereum-optimism/optimism#22668 and ethereum-optimism/specs#935.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-27T18:27:40Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 584,
      "deletions": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs8AAAABD_rE0A",
      "title": "feat(standard-versions): add final op-contracts/v7.0.0 and v8.0.0 entries",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1340,
      "body": "Adds the final (non-rc) `op-contracts/v7.0.0` and `op-contracts/v8.0.0` entries to `standard-versions-mainnet.toml` and `standard-versions-sepolia.toml`, keeping the existing rc entries.\r\n\r\n## Background\r\n\r\n`op-contracts/v8.0.0` was tagged today by @maurelian at the same commit as `v8.0.0-rc.3` (`f45a5cc`); `op-contracts/v7.0.0` exists at the same commit as `v7.0.0-rc.4` (`a7c88c8`) but was never added to the registry. Contracts were not redeployed in either case, so addresses and versions are identical to the rc blocks. \r\n\r\nReleases:\r\n- https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/releases/tag/op-contracts%2Fv7.0.0\r\n- https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/releases/tag/op-contracts%2Fv8.0.0\r\n\r\nSupersedes #1338, which renamed the `v8.0.0-rc.3` entry in place instead of adding a new block.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-17T21:16:30Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-09-17T21:35:31Z",
      "additions": 84,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
